<title>ESTONIA: RATING WILL BE GOOD FOR HOIUBANK - ANALYSTS.</title>
<headline>RATING WILL BE GOOD FOR HOIUBANK - ANALYSTS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts said on Monday that Hoiubank's decision to seek a rating from Moody's will have a positive impact on the bank's long-term development.</p>
<p>Analysts said the bank could get cheaper foreign loans and a possible share issue in foreign markets could also be done They added it will have a long-term impact on the share price, but were not sure on the short-term impact.</p>
<p>&quot;In the short-term it is hard to say how the stock will move,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>Analysts were also unsure about what rating Hoiubank will obtain.</p>
<p>&quot;The grade depends on the country rating, the bank cannot be given a higher rating than the country,&quot; an analyst said.</p>
<p>Estonia's central bank said last week that it will probably seek a country rating from Moody's.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
